    {
        "content": "<p>I'm also wondering if it would be possible to multiply elements of <code>DMatrix</code> under certain conditions (I think that the minimum requirement for multiplication to be defined is that <code>α</code> is the <code>Hom</code> function for some preadditive category, as this would make <code>DMatrix</code> similar to <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=CategoryTheory.Mat_#doc\">docs#CategoryTheory.Mat_</a>)</p>",
        "id": 580973535,
        "sender_full_name": "Niels Voss",
        "timestamp": 1774227475
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Do we have the linear category structure on <code>Mat_</code>?</p>\n<p>I suspect that setting up multiplication on <code>DMatrix</code> essentially amounts to re-inventing preadditive / linear categories, and it might just be easier to work with <code>Mat_</code>.</p>",
        "id": 581010576,
        "sender_full_name": "Kim Morrison",
        "timestamp": 1774241003
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Interestingly, the reason I asked this question was because I need a computable version of <code>Mat_</code> (see this thread: <a class=\"stream-topic\" data-stream-id=\"287929\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Design.20of.20CategoryTheory.2EMat_.20and.20CategoryTheory.2EMat/with/580982342\">#mathlib4 &gt; Design of CategoryTheory.Mat_ and CategoryTheory.Mat</a>). And in order to do that I need the module structure on <code>DMatrix</code> (I don't need the multiplication on DMatrix).</p>\n<p>As far as I can tell, there's no linear category on <code>Mat_</code></p>",
        "id": 581011198,
        "sender_full_name": "Niels Voss",
        "timestamp": 1774241328
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=DMatrix#doc\">docs#DMatrix</a></p>",
        "id": 581070622,
        "sender_full_name": "Edward van de Meent",
        "timestamp": 1774261580
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Looks like you want <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Pi.module#doc\">docs#Pi.module</a> (modulo default transparency)?<br>\ni.e. something like</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">module</span>\n<span class=\"n\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Defs</span>\n<span class=\"n\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Data</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Matrix</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">DMatrix</span>\n<span class=\"n\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Pi</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Semiring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">AddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">DMatrix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inferInstanceAs</span><span class=\"bp\">%</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
